    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **65 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured `OWNER_CREATED` audit event on owner creation, satisfying checkpoint `cp53`.\n\n**What changed (3 files):**\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `getPrimaryIdentifier()` accessor (`@Transient`, matching the existing derived-getter convention) that returns `customerCode` today. This is the single point of change: when the customer code is later unified into the memberId, only this method changes and the audit event carries the memberId automatically \u2014 exactly the forward-looking requirement in the spec.\n\n2. **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** (new) \u2014 an immutable `record(seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel)` holding the `OWNER_CREATED` marker. It stamps a process-wide, monotonically increasing `seq` via a static `AtomicLong` (`next(owner)`) sourced from `owner.getPrimaryIdentifier()`, and renders compact JSON in spec order: `{\"seq\":..,\"ownerId\":..,\"customerCode\":..,\"membershipLevel\":..,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` (with proper string escaping).\n\n3. **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 after the existing human-readable audit line, emits the structured event to the same `AUDIT` logger via `AUDIT.info(\"{}\", OwnerCreatedEvent.next(owner).toJson())`. Passing the JSON as a single SLF4J argument keeps the braces from being treated as placeholders.\n\nThe observed output confirms both lines and the increasing `seq`:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - owner created id=11 customerCode=NSW-16E6609E ...\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\nNo YAML wiring changes were needed since the emission lives in the existing `audit` pipeline step. The new `cp53` test and the existing audit tests (`cp21`, `cp43`) all pass, and the full suite of 65 tests is green.",
